# T1 -- PHOTON kinetic Hessian on the disformal metric g~ = eta + B u u  (is the photon a ghost?)
####################################################################################################
   g~ determinant  det g~ = B - 1   (Lorentzian iff <0)
   electric Hessian diag  H_ii = 1/sqrt(1 - B)  (x3, isotropic)
     B=0.00:  det g~=-1.0000 (Lorentzian:True)   H_electric=+1.0000 (ghost-free:True)
     B=0.30:  det g~=-0.7000 (Lorentzian:True)   H_electric=+1.1952 (ghost-free:True)
     B=0.60:  det g~=-0.4000 (Lorentzian:True)   H_electric=+1.5811 (ghost-free:True)
     B=0.90:  det g~=-0.1000 (Lorentzian:True)   H_electric=+3.1623 (ghost-free:True)
     B=0.99:  det g~=-0.0100 (Lorentzian:True)   H_electric=+10.0000 (ghost-free:True)
   [PASS] PHOTON: for physical 0<=B<1, g~ Lorentzian AND electric Hessian>0 -> photon not a ghost (computed)
   [PASS] PHOTON: the causal bound B<1 EMERGES (at B>=1 det g~ ceases Lorentzian / kinetic lost)
   => B<1 is the subluminal/Lorentzian window, derived from the Hessian, not imposed.

